<title>CANADA: Eldorado, HRC merger approved.</title>
<headline>Eldorado, HRC merger approved.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eldorado Gold Corp and HRC Development Corp said Friday that shareholders for both mining companies have approved an amalgamation of the two firms.</p>
<p>The new company will be called Eldorado Gold Corp, the companies said in a release.</p>
<p>The amalgamated company is a fully integrated gold producer with plans to grow through exploration and acquisiton. Its major shareholder is international mining giant Gencor Ltd .</p>
<p>The company said it plans to produce 500,000 ounces of gold annually within five years and one million ounces a year within 10 years.</p>
<p>--Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
</text>
